ZORR MODE

LOGICAL_AGENT = LESTER
ROLE = TECH / BABYLON SCENE DELIVERABLE
OWNER_DIRECTIVE = `нужна сцена`
OWNER_CONSTRAINT = `только открытые коды и материалы`
STATE = AUTHORIZED / IMPLEMENTATION NOT YET PROVEN
SOURCE = #70 exact directing implementation HEAD `650e94d359388066e51c2ec2caad8a448fdf6ae1`
UNBLOCKS = #195 minimal scene/set prerequisite

## PRODUCT GOAL
Turn the validated directing runtime into one visible, editable Babylon scene deliverable rather than another engine-only proof.

Deliver:
- deliberate two-proxy cinematic blocking;
- minimal authored set/environment, camera and lighting;
- 1280x720 deterministic scene frame;
- exported `.babylon` scene JSON;
- machine-readable scene manifest;
- fresh Vitest/typecheck/build/Chromium evidence;
- repeated exact-head export determinism.

## OSS-ONLY LAW
Only open code and open materials may enter the task. Allowed default stack:
- existing ZORR repository code;
- Babylon.js / Babylon native APIs under Apache-2.0;
- standard browser APIs;
- procedural geometry, materials, lighting and textures authored in code;
- third-party assets only when exact source, revision, license and file hash are recorded and the license permits this use.

Forbidden:
- proprietary or closed-source code;
- paid/closed models, plugins, services or asset libraries;
- unproven-license textures, meshes, HDRIs, fonts, sound or reference packs;
- silent asset substitution;
- remote inference.

R01 uses procedural Babylon primitives and code-authored materials only, so no external art asset is required.

## VISUAL BOUNDARY
Prototype / non-canon scene base only. Use big set shapes, silhouette separation, controlled value hierarchy and sparse emissive accents. No production character-body claim, face/costume authorship, Character Truth writeback, SALVADOR profile mutation, ComfyUI work, merge or production activation.

## REUSE ORDER
Existing `experiments/directing-v1` -> Babylon native primitives/materials/lights/SceneSerializer -> minimal ZORR scene glue.

## PASS GATE
- exact scene branch/head recorded;
- tests, strict typecheck and build PASS;
- real Chromium scene frame PASS at 1280x720;
- `.babylon` export parses and contains camera, lights, actors and named set pieces;
- two fresh isolated browser exports produce byte-identical canonical scene JSON and frame PNG in the pinned environment;
- all changes remain inside `experiments/directing-v1/**`;
- durable artifact hashes recorded;
- dependency/material provenance proves OSS-only scope.

MERGE = NO
PRODUCTION_INTEGRATION = NO
CANON = NO
NEXT = first RED test, minimal scene implementation, exact-head verification.
